# Hono Workers Vitest (Cloudflare pool)

Pinned here: vitest 4.1.x, @cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers 0.21.x, hono 4.13.x, wrangler 4.120.x, worker-api compatibility_date 2026-07-08 with nodejs_compat.
General Vitest agent bar: [vitest.mdc](vitest.mdc). Discipline: [testing.mdc](../quality/testing.mdc).
Docs retrieved 2026-08-11: Cloudflare Vitest integration (configuration, test APIs, isolation, migrate Vitest 3 to 4), Hono testing guide. Prefer those over training memory.

## 1. Scope

Governs Vitest for Hono apps on Cloudflare Workers using @cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers (workerd), not Node Vitest.
Typical paths: apps/worker-*/tests/**, apps/worker-*/vitest.config.*, same for queue-*/webhook-*/mcp-* when added.

## 2. Toolchain and canonical config

Canonical pattern (matches apps/worker-api/vitest.config.mts):

```ts
import { defineWorkersConfig } from "@repo/vitest-config/workers";

export default defineWorkersConfig({
  wrangler: { configPath: "./wrangler.jsonc" },
});
```

defineWorkersConfig wraps cloudflareTest() plus shared mock hygiene from @repo/vitest-config. Import the Workers entry (@repo/vitest-config/workers), not the Node entry.

Divergences from Node Vitest (do not paper over):
- Test files run inside workerd; the Vitest config and globalSetup run in Node.
- Use cloudflareTest() Vite plugin (via defineWorkersConfig). The old Cloudflare helpers defineWorkersConfig / defineWorkersProject from @cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers/config are removed (Vitest 4 / pool-workers >= 0.13) - do not confuse them with this repo's @repo/vitest-config/workers export.
- Options formerly under test.poolOptions.workers pass directly to cloudflareTest() / defineWorkersConfig().
- Pool injects minimal Node-compat flags for Vitest unless wrangler already defines a Node.js compatibility flag (isolation-and-concurrency docs).
- compatibility_date and compatibility_flags come from wrangler.jsonc via wrangler.configPath. Prerequisite: compatibility_date >= 2022-10-31, ES modules format. This repo sets nodejs_compat on worker apps - keep it; do not invent extra flags unless wrangler needs them.
- Optional miniflare key merges over wrangler; miniflare wins on conflicts (e.g. stub a service binding only in tests).
- Never set isolate: false / Node pool on Workers configs (shares binding storage).
- Types: tests/tsconfig.json should include @cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers/types and committed worker-configuration.d.ts (in include). Ambient typing:

```ts
declare module "cloudflare:workers" {
  interface ProvidedEnv extends Env {}
}
```

(as in apps/worker-api/tests/env.d.ts)

## 3. Runtime model and isolation

Bindings and Worker entry:
- Prefer import { env, exports } from "cloudflare:workers".
- env / SELF from cloudflare:test are deprecated; exports.default.fetch() replaces SELF.fetch(). exports does not expose Assets - use env.ASSETS or startDevWorker for assets.
- Helpers remain on cloudflare:test: createExecutionContext, waitOnExecutionContext, createScheduledController, createMessageBatch, getQueueResult, Durable Object helpers, applyD1Migrations, reset, Workflow introspectors.
- fetchMock from cloudflare:test is removed - mock globalThis.fetch or use MSW.

Isolation (Cloudflare isolation-and-concurrency + Vitest 4 migration):
- Storage isolation is per test file by default. Files run concurrently. Writes in one file are not visible to another.
- Within a file, storage persists across it() unless you call await reset() (e.g. afterEach).
- isolatedStorage and singleWorker config options are removed.

| Mode | How | Tradeoff |
|------|-----|----------|
| Default | no special flags | Isolated storage per file, concurrent - prefer this |
| Single process | --max-workers=1 | Still isolated storage; shared worker process |
| Shared storage | --max-workers=1 --no-isolate | Shared globals and storage across files - order-dependent; avoid unless intentional |

Vitest general advice to disable isolate for speed also shares Workers binding storage - never apply casually to storage-backed tests.

workerd do / do not:
- Do use real local bindings from wrangler / miniflare simulation.
- Do assert on Response status/body/headers and binding state.
- Do not use removed fetchMock; mock globalThis.fetch or MSW instead.
- Do not assume vi.mock intercepts the main Worker entry - the pool injects a side-effect import of main outside normal mock setup (workers-sdk pool notes).
- Do not set Node pool threads/forks on Workers configs.

.dev.vars (explicit uncertainty):
Docs retrieved for this rule document .dev.vars for wrangler/vite local development and secrets.required, but do not clearly state that vitest-pool-workers always loads .dev.vars the same way. Prefer miniflare.bindings or wrangler vars for CI-stable secrets in tests. Never commit .dev.vars. Do not write tests that only pass when a local secret file is present.

## 4. Testing Hono

Hono export default app is the Worker entry (apps/worker-api/src/index.ts).

| Mode | Pattern | When |
|------|---------|------|
| Unit / route-focused | await app.request(path, init?, env?) - 3rd arg sets c.env | Middleware isolation, intentional mock env, no full export path |
| Integration | await exports.default.fetch(request) | Full default export + real pool env |
| Handler + waitUntil | worker.fetch(req, env, createExecutionContext()) then waitOnExecutionContext | Side effects via waitUntil |

Repo default for gateway smoke: exports integration (see apps/worker-api/tests/routes/health.test.ts). Use app.request when stubbing c.env without exercising real storage bindings. Optional testClient from hono/testing is secondary.

Hono docs: pass MOCK_ENV as the 3rd parameter to app.request for bindings. Prefer real env from cloudflare:workers when the behavior under test depends on KV/D1/R2/DO/queues.

## 5. Durable Objects and D1

worker-api has neither today. Document for future worker-* apps. APIs from Cloudflare Test APIs docs.

runInDurableObject(stub, callback) - run inside the DO instance to seed/inspect storage or call methods. Avoids guessing state only through fetch/RPC.

```ts
import { env } from "cloudflare:workers";
import { runInDurableObject } from "cloudflare:test";

const id = env.COUNTER.newUniqueId();
const stub = env.COUNTER.get(id);
await runInDurableObject(stub, async (instance, state) => {
  await state.storage.put("count", 1);
});
```

runDurableObjectAlarm(stub) - immediately run and clear a scheduled alarm; returns whether an alarm ran. Avoids waiting on real alarm timers.

listDurableObjectIds(namespace) - IDs created in this test file only (respects per-file isolation).

evictDurableObject / evictAllDurableObjects - tear down in-memory DO instances while preserving durable storage (available in pool-workers >= 0.16.20; this repo is 0.21). Use to test recovery across eviction.

applyD1Migrations(db, migrations, tableName?) - apply migrations in tests. Read migrations in Node via readD1Migrations from @cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers/config inside cloudflareTest(async () => ...), pass via miniflare.bindings, apply in a setupFile.

Workflow introspectors (introspectWorkflowInstance / introspectWorkflow): must dispose with await using or dispose(), or instance state leaks across tests (false greens).

## 6. Gotchas (false greens first)

| Gotcha | Why | Correct pattern | Source |
|--------|-----|-----------------|--------|
| import { SELF, env } from cloudflare:test / SELF.fetch | Deprecated; Assets semantics differ | import { env, exports } from cloudflare:workers; exports.default.fetch | migrate Vitest 3 to 4 |
| fetchMock from cloudflare:test | Removed | mock globalThis.fetch or MSW | migrate Vitest 3 to 4 |
| expect(x).toBeDefined() only | Passes for almost anything | Assert status, parsed body, headers, binding effects | Vitest Writing Tests with AI |
| Assume storage cleared per it() | Isolation is per file | await reset() in afterEach when needed | Test APIs reset |
| --no-isolate / isolate: false for speed | Shares Workers binding storage | Keep default isolation for storage tests | Vitest perf + Cloudflare migration |
| Mock KV/D1/R2 instead of pool bindings | Tests pass with stubs that diverge from workerd | Use wrangler/miniflare real local bindings | write-your-first-test |
| Workflow introspector not disposed | State leaks - next test sees completed instance | await using or dispose() | Test APIs Workflows |
| vi.mock on Worker main entry | Pool injects main outside mock graph | Prefer exports.fetch + binding APIs; mock outbound fetch | workers-sdk pool notes |
| Assert Assets via exports.default.fetch | exports does not expose Assets | env.ASSETS or startDevWorker | Test APIs exports |
| Hono app.request with MOCK_ENV only, claiming binding correctness | Never hits real binding semantics | Use env from cloudflare:workers for binding behavior | Hono testing + Cloudflare env |
| Test depends on local .dev.vars | CI/agents without the file get different results | miniflare.bindings / wrangler vars; flag if undocumented | wrangler secrets docs; pool docs silent |
| Unawaited async in tests | Unhandled rejection / flaky pass | await; expect(...).rejects | Vitest common-errors |
| Set Node pool threads on Workers config | Does not select Cloudflare pool | cloudflareTest only | Vitest common-errors / pool model |
| jest.fn / jest.mock | Wrong API | vi.* | Vitest Writing Tests with AI |

## 7. CI and performance

- CI: pnpm turbo run test --affected (.github/workflows/ci.yml). Package scripts use vitest run. No pool-specific shard flags today.
- Default: concurrent files, per-file storage isolation.
- Shared storage only with --max-workers=1 --no-isolate - not for routine CI.
- Vitest --shard + blob merge is documented by Vitest at file granularity. Compatibility with vitest-pool-workers is not claimed in Cloudflare docs retrieved 2026-08-11 - keep CI unsharded unless proven.
- Do not claim Node execArgv --cpu-prof profiles workerd runners (not in retrieved Cloudflare docs). Use Vitest duration metrics, optional importDurations, and turbo --filter while iterating.

## 8. Anti-patterns (never generate)

- defineWorkersConfig / defineWorkersProject / test.poolOptions.workers nesting
- isolatedStorage or singleWorker options on cloudflareTest
- import { SELF, fetchMock } from "cloudflare:test"
- jest.* APIs
- Stubbing KV/D1/R2/DO that the pool would simulate locally
- Weak assertions (toBeDefined-only) or asserting workerd-private internals
- Logging or asserting privileged client/matter identifiers (see guardrails)
- Silencing failing tests (skip, any-cast, loosened types)
- Node environment Vitest for Worker apps
- Starting vitest watch / --ui from an agent session
- Adding @vitest/ui unsolicited

## 9. Self-verification checklist

- [ ] vitest.config uses defineWorkersConfig from @repo/vitest-config/workers + wrangler.configPath (not obsolete Cloudflare defineWorkers*)
- [ ] tests/env.d.ts ProvidedEnv extends Env; tests tsconfig types include @cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers/types; check-types runs tests/tsconfig
- [ ] Isolation assumptions match (per-file; reset/dispose if needed)
- [ ] Binding use is real pool vs intentional Hono MOCK_ENV - stated in the test purpose
- [ ] Hono unit (app.request) vs integration (exports.default.fetch) choice is justified
- [ ] DO/D1/Workflow helpers used with dispose/reset where required
- [ ] Assertions check observable behavior (status, contract body, headers)
- [ ] vitest run via pnpm turbo run test --filter=<app> passes without relying on local .dev.vars
